{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nSITE: `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` `run_sweep(tracker)` — `repo_root = os.path.dirname(tracker)`, sanctioned `# repo-root-ok:` in the AC#3 guard (`scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`) as the ONE deferred CONFIG-ROOT site.\n\nCONTEXT: split off from auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7-be89-9b01-496a), which fixed the 8 clean `dirname(tracker)`-as-config-root sites. `run_sweep` is the DETACHED-CHILD compaction entry point: spawned with cwd == the canonical STORE, inheriting only `tracker`. auspicial DEFERRED this site because the detached child needs a DURABLE code root and the two supported topologies (relocated store vs. co-located worktree symlink) disagree on how to derive it.\n\nIMPACT (milder than the parent's AC#1): on a relocated store (`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` — the deployed MCP topology, store `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, code `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`) `run_sweep` reads DEFAULT compaction config (threshold 10, 1800 s horizon) instead of the project's `[compact]` block. Compaction still runs; it folds the right tickets by the WRONG rule. No gate is disabled.\n\n## The fix (operator-approved; supersedes the deferral)\n\nAdd a dedicated leaf resolver `compaction_child_repo_root(canonical_tracker)` in `_config_resolvers.py` with precedence: explicit `REBAR_ROOT` (realpath) if set → else `dirname(canonical tracker)`. `run_sweep` calls it as `compaction_child_repo_root(StorePaths(tracker).canonical)` and the `# repo-root-ok:` sanction is removed.\n\nCorrect for BOTH topologies WITHOUT depending on the child's cwd: deployment exports `REBAR_ROOT` unconditionally (first arm); local `make worktree` resolves via the fallback, where `StorePaths(tracker).canonical` realpath-resolves the `.tickets-tracker` symlink back to the durable main checkout (bugs 3198/93a9). Full design rationale, rejected alternatives (threading the caller's root; `repo_root_or_none()`'s git-toplevel-of-cwd arm; `snapshot_repo_root()`), topology detail, ADR 0051 relation, and the flowered-basaltic-beagle (088b-e4c1-050c-4516) non-overlap are recorded in a ticket comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC#1 — `run_sweep` resolves the code/config root independent of store location via `compaction_child_repo_root(StorePaths(tracker).canonical)` (precedence `REBAR_ROOT` realpath > `dirname(canonical tracker)`). No spawn-contract change; no caller-threaded root; no `repo_root_or_none()` git-toplevel arm; no `snapshot_repo_root()`. Proven by AC#2's seam assertion.\n- [ ] AC#2a — On a relocated store (external `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`, `REBAR_ROOT` set to the checkout) with a non-default `[compact]` block, `run_sweep` honours it (RED->GREEN). Config comes from a `rebar.toml` FILE, never `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD` / `REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS` (an env read is root-independent and would hide the bug). Proved by `tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py::test_run_sweep_folds_by_the_repo_compact_config_on_relocated_store`.\n- [ ] AC#2b — The root `run_sweep` hands `compact_all_cli` IS the resolved code root, pinned at the seam, so a fix that merely lands on a root reading the same config by accident is still caught. Proved by `::test_run_sweep_hands_the_resolved_code_root_to_the_sweep`.\n- [ ] AC#3 — The `# repo-root-ok:` sanction is removed from `compact_trigger.py`, leaving the guard allowlist with ZERO deferred config-root sites (only `_store/sync.py`'s `tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote` reads remain, legitimately rooted in the STORE's own git repo). Proved by `tests/unit/test_repo_root_from_tracker_guard.py::test_no_config_root_site_is_deferred_behind_a_sanction` and `python scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py` exiting 0.\n- [ ] AC#4 — The FALLBACK arm is exercised: with `REBAR_ROOT` UNSET and a real `.tickets-tracker` SYMLINK store, `dirname(canonical tracker)` resolves the symlink back to the durable checkout and reaches the code root, pinned at the seam (NOT the ephemeral worktree dir). Proved by `::test_run_sweep_resolves_the_code_root_without_rebar_root`.\n- [ ] AC#5 — A config-effect contrast shows the fold reads the repo config, not an unconditional sweep: the same store/ticket fold NOTHING under a `[compact]` block whose horizon puts the events out of reach. The HORIZON is the discriminator, not the threshold (`compact_plan.needs_folding` BACKFILL arm selects any snapshot-less ticket with ≥1 foldable event whatever the threshold). LIVENESS (the sweep actually REACHED `compact_all_cli`) is asserted separately from the seam and the no-snapshot outcome — `run_sweep` swallows every exception, so an absent snapshot would otherwise be satisfied by a crash. Proved by `::test_run_sweep_respects_a_repo_config_that_folds_nothing`.\n- [ ] AC#6 — Caused-by attribution: same origin class as the parent (`dirname(tracker)`-as-config-root construct); this site was written by `d2dea317ec94` (rebar-ticket `1fde-becd-942a-4351`), recorded as a `caused_by` link.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun every command from the change's worktree with its venv first on `PATH`.\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py tests/unit/test_repo_root_from_tracker_guard.py tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py -q --color=no` — the relocated-store fold and the seam assertion are RED before the fix and GREEN after; the guard self-test reports no deferred config-root site; the existing trigger suite does not regress.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py` — exits 0 on the drained tree (AC#3).\n- Sandboxed mutation check (macOS `sandbox-exec`), each mutant applied then reverted: (1) `repo_root = os.path.dirname(tracker)` returns all four run_sweep tests to RED; (2) `repo_root = None` leaves the pure-fold test GREEN (`compose_config(None)` rediscovers `REBAR_ROOT`) and is caught ONLY by the three seam-bearing tests; (3) `os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(tracker))` (dropping `REBAR_ROOT` precedence) is killed by the relocated-store tests and survives ONLY the symlink test — demonstrating both precedence arms are needed.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && make typecheck` — no regressions.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py -q --color=no` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` — the CI-only module-size gate and the complexity ratchet stay clean (`new=0 increased=0`)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787957758037638001,"uuid":"11f03eda-7d68-4427-8d48-ccc9752e33b0"}